  "rationale": "The cited Shared Value, State, Give, Eval/EvalArgs, Pattern/Bind and ExprTyped/ArgsTyped are used directly by Functions, not redefined under changed behavior. The appendix table matches the inherited units reviewed as context: kinds, modes on references, partial views, move/copy/promotion, whole constructor arguments, shared-struct initial mode, and unique-only unpack. It accurately distinguishes reuse of the call-free foundation from the new call syntax/frame machine and makes no claim that full call safety was proved. The machine/gc/steps units introduce the lifetime notation; inherited syntax, storage and typing notation remain in the listed dependency units. Functions keeps its explicit inherited-machinery forward reference to the appendix.",
